242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (The initial dataset obtained after the scraping process contained 20,000 observations and seven variables, including cruise name, ship, company, price, duration, start date, and end date. Although the dataset appeared complete at first glance, further inspection revealed several data quality issues that required preprocessing before analysis.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (A major issue identified in the dataset was the presence of duplicate records. More than half of the observations were duplicated, which likely resulted from overlapping data across multiple scraped pages. Retaining duplicate entries would have distorted any further analysis by overrepresenting certain cruises. Therefore, duplicate rows were removed to ensure that each observation corresponded to a unique cruise entry. After this step, the index was reset to maintain a clean and consistent structure.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (Another issue concerned missing values in the price variable. While the majority of the dataset was complete, a small number of entries had missing price information. Since the proportion of missing values was relatively low, these values were imputed using the median of the price distribution. The choice of the median was appropriate because it is less sensitive to extreme values and preserves the overall distribution of the data more effectively than the mean.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (The date variables required substantial cleaning due to inconsistencies in formatting. The original data contained additional text preceding the actual dates, as well as month names written in Russian abbreviations. Furthermore, some entries did not include the year. These inconsistencies were addressed by removing unnecessary prefixes, translating month names into English, and appending a default year where it was missing. After these transformations, both date columns were converted into a standard datetime format, allowing for proper chronological ordering and enabling time-based analysis.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
