249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 218 0 R
/T (The ship variable also contained redundant textual prefixes that did not contribute meaningful information. These prefixes were removed to simplify the data and improve readability. This step ensured that the values in the column represented only the ship names without unnecessary repetition.)
/E (The ship variable also contained redundant textual prefixes that did not contribute meaningful information. These prefixes were removed to simplify the data and improve readability. This step ensured that the values in the column represented only the ship names without unnecessary repetition.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 218 0 R
/T (Another important aspect of preprocessing involved addressing language inconsistencies. The dataset contained a mixture of Russian and English text, particularly in the cruise names. To ensure uniformity and facilitate analysis, the cruise names were translated into English. This step improved the interpretability of the data and made it suitable for further text-based processing.)
/E (Another important aspect of preprocessing involved addressing language inconsistencies. The dataset contained a mixture of Russian and English text, particularly in the cruise names. To ensure uniformity and facilitate analysis, the cruise names were translated into English. This step improved the interpretability of the data and made it suitable for further text-based processing.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
